menu "Layout Types"

config NVMEM_LAYOUT_QCOM_ETH_MAC
	tristate "Qualcomm Ethernet MAC address layout"
	depends on OF
	help
	  Handles the non-contiguous eFuse storage of eth MAC byte[5]
	  on Qualcomm SoC. Provides transparent post-processing for
	  the ethx-mac nvmem cell.

	  Say Y if you use the SA8797P SoC with Ethernet.

config NVMEM_LAYOUT_U_BOOT_ENV
	tristate "U-Boot environment variables layout"
	select CRC32
	select GENERIC_NET_UTILS
	help
	  U-Boot stores its setup as environment variables. This driver adds
	  support for verifying & exporting such data. It also exposes variables
	  as NVMEM cells so they can be referenced by other drivers.

	  If unsure, say N.

endmenu
